
PREFIX="fdagcp"
PROJECT="${PREFIX}-audit-logs"
SA_NAME="splunk-gcp"
SA_EMAIL="${SA_NAME}@${PROJECT}.iam.gserviceaccount.com"
POOL_ID="splunk-aws"
PROVIDER_ID="aws"
SUB="all-logs-splunk"
TOPIC="all-logs"
AWS_ACCOUNT="123456789012"          # from Brian / AWS
AWS_ROLE="splunk-gcp-pubsub"        # IAM role on the Splunk host
IMPERSONATE="${PREFIX}-bootstrap@${PREFIX}-iac-core.iam.gserviceaccount.com"
ORG_ID="854264547149"

gcloud config set project "${PROJECT}"
PROJECT_NUMBER="$(gcloud projects describe "${PROJECT}" --format='value(projectNumber)')"
. Org sink and subscription (0-bootstrap)
In fast/stages-aw/0-bootstrap/terraform.tfvars, keep audit-logs, vpc-sc, and workspace-audit-logs. Add all-logs. Do not drop existing keys.
all-logs = {
  filter = ""
  type   = "pubsub"
}
cd fast/stages-aw/0-bootstrap
terraform plan
# expect CREATE topic all-logs, subscription all-logs-splunk, org sink all-logs
# no DESTROY of the three logging sinks
terraform apply
gcloud logging sinks describe all-logs --organization="${ORG_ID}" \
  --format="yaml(name,destination,includeChildren,writerIdentity)"

gcloud pubsub topics describe "${TOPIC}" --project="${PROJECT}"
gcloud pubsub subscriptions describe "${SUB}" --project="${PROJECT}"
Expect destination pubsub.googleapis.com/projects/${PROJECT}/topics/all-logs, includeChildren: true, subscription retention 604800s (7 days).

2. Splunk service account (no key)
gcloud iam service-accounts create "${SA_NAME}" \
  --project="${PROJECT}" \
  --display-name="Splunk Pub/Sub pull" \
  --description="WIF from AWS; pull all-logs-splunk"
Do not create a JSON key.

3. Workload Identity Pool (AWS)
gcloud iam workload-identity-pools create "${POOL_ID}" \
  --project="${PROJECT}" \
  --location=global \
  --display-name="Splunk AWS Pub/Sub pull"

gcloud iam workload-identity-pools providers create-aws "${PROVIDER_ID}" \
  --project="${PROJECT}" \
  --location=global \
  --workload-identity-pool="${POOL_ID}" \
  --account-id="${AWS_ACCOUNT}" \
  --attribute-mapping="google.subject=assertion.arn,attribute.account=assertion.account,attribute.aws_role=assertion.arn.contains('assumed-role') ? assertion.arn.extract('{account_arn}assumed-role/{role_name}/') : assertion.arn" \
  --attribute-condition="attribute.aws_role=='arn:aws:sts::${AWS_ACCOUNT}:assumed-role/${AWS_ROLE}'"
Do not reuse the bootstrap GitHub/GitLab pool. The attribute condition is required so the whole AWS account cannot impersonate the SA.
4. Let that AWS role impersonate the GCP SA
gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding "${SA_EMAIL}" \
  --project="${PROJECT}" \
  --role="roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser" \
  --member="principalSet://iam.googleapis.com/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/${POOL_ID}/attribute.aws_role/arn:aws:sts::${AWS_ACCOUNT}:assumed-role/${AWS_ROLE}"

5. Pub/Sub IAM
gcloud pubsub subscriptions add-iam-policy-binding "${SUB}" \
  --project="${PROJECT}" \
  --member="serviceAccount:${SA_EMAIL}" \
  --role="roles/pubsub.subscriber"

gcloud pubsub topics add-iam-policy-binding "${TOPIC}" \
  --project="${PROJECT}" \
  --member="serviceAccount:${SA_EMAIL}" \
  --role="roles/pubsub.viewer"
Confirm the Logging sink writer still has roles/pubsub.publisher on the topic (Terraform set that).
6. VPC-SC (3-security)
pubsub.googleapis.com is restricted. fdagcp-audit-logs is in platform. Splunk/AWS is outside, so pull is denied until ingress exists.
Get the project number from step 0. In live 3-security terraform.tfvars, add next to terraform-operators (the key attaches to platform by itself):
splunk-pubsub-pull = {
  from = {
    access_levels = ["*"]
    identities = [
      "serviceAccount:splunk-gcp@fdagcp-audit-logs.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
    ]
  }
  to = {
    operations = [
      {
        service_name     = "pubsub.googleapis.com"
        method_selectors = ["*"]
      },
    ]
    resources = ["projects/<AUDIT_PROJECT_NUMBER>"]
  }
}
access_levels = ["*"] is required (AWS is on the internet).
If operators still cannot run gcloud pubsub / WIF IAM from a laptop, add the same services plus iam.googleapis.com for group:RB-FDAIT-GCP-org-admins@fda.hhs.gov (the splunk-setup policy from earlier).
. Credential config for AWS (not a key)
gcloud iam workload-identity-pools create-cred-config \
  "projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/${POOL_ID}/providers/${PROVIDER_ID}" \
  --service-account="${SA_EMAIL}" \
  --aws \
  --output-file=./splunk-aws-credential-config.json
Give Brian that file. It is WIF config (pool, provider, SA). It is not private_key.

8. AWS / Splunk host
On the Splunk HF / IDM that runs the GCP add-on:
1. Instance profile / assumed role must be arn:aws:sts::${AWS_ACCOUNT}:assumed-role/${AWS_ROLE}.
2. Place the config file and point ADC at it:
sudo mkdir -p /opt/splunk/etc/apps/Splunk_TA_google-cloudplatform/local/
sudo cp splunk-aws-credential-config.json /opt/splunk/etc/apps/Splunk_TA_google-cloudplatform/local/
sudo chown splunk:splunk /opt/splunk/etc/apps/Splunk_TA_google-cloudplatform/local/splunk-aws-credential-config.json
export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/opt/splunk/etc/apps/Splunk_TA_google-cloudplatform/local/splunk-aws-credential-config.json
Persist that env for the Splunk process (systemd drop-in or splunk-launch.conf), then restart Splunk.
1. Splunk Add-on for Google Cloud Platform 4.x+, input type Pub/Sub pull (not HEC):
Field	Value
Project	fdagcp-audit-logs
Subscription	all-logs-splunk
Authentication	Application Default Credentials / WIF (no JSON key)
9. Prove it
From the AWS host as that role:
gcloud pubsub subscriptions pull all-logs-splunk \
  --project=fdagcp-audit-logs \
  --limit=1 \
  --auto-ack=false
In GCP:
gcloud pubsub subscriptions describe all-logs-splunk \
  --project=fdagcp-audit-logs \
  --format="yaml(name,topic,numUndeliveredMessages,ackDeadlineSeconds,messageRetentionDuration)"
In Splunk, search the index the add-on writes. If GCP has undelivered messages and Splunk is empty, check VPC-SC denies on pubsub.googleapis.com for splunk-gcp@…, then WIF (sts.googleapis.com / iamcredentials.googleapis.com). If both APIs are denied, add them to the same ingress as Pub/Sub.

What each piece does
Piece	Who creates it	Purpose
Org sink all-logs	Terraform 0-bootstrap	Writes org logs to the topic
Topic all-logs + sub all-logs-splunk	Terraform 0-bootstrap	Buffer (7-day unacked)
SA splunk-gcp@	gcloud (not Terraform)	Identity Splunk impersonates
WIF pool/provider	gcloud	Trust that one AWS role; no SA key
Pub/Sub IAM	gcloud	Subscriber on the subscription
VPC-SC ingress	Terraform 3-security	Allow that SA to call Pub/Sub from AWS
Do not grant roles/pubsub.admin or project Owner to Splunk. Do not bind principalSet://…/workloadIdentityPools/splunk-aws/*. Unacked messages last 7 days; finish Splunk config in the same window as the sink.




